From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:26:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: hold a station that stops answering while awake
 to the firmware

A phone asleep sends its keepalives from its Wi-Fi chip, between a null
frame that says it is awake and one that says it dozes again. When the
last one doesn't arrive, the firmware has the phone awake for as long as
it stays silent, and every frame handed to the hardware for it in that
time is lost: sent in vain, or given back without having been sent. No
power-save report comes.

Once a frame to a station of an AP interface comes back failed and
nothing has been heard from the station for a while (no frame, no ACK,
no power-save report), or a few frames in a row come back failed, hold
it as a dozing station is held, with nothing handed to the hardware: its
frames wait in its queues. The next frame received from it, the next
power-save report or an ACK releases it. A null frame sent at growing
intervals is the probe that finds a station which does listen and only
had nothing to say.

silent_hold (module parameter, on by default) switches it off. The
station's debugfs ps file shows the holds, their time and the probes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mac80211.c       |  18 +++
 mt76.h           |  32 +++++
 mt7915/debugfs.c |  20 +++-
 mt7915/mac.c     |   8 ++
 tx.c             | 306 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 382 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

